{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0EZN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$H^i(S_\\etale, \\mathcal{F}) = 0$", "MATH_0005": "$i > 0$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-only-closed-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:62ea400a66824cfc71ab7426ae09ac063f6ae411064627ee5f4b8da3b518e5a1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:63ef9e054a69ce5ba189997ff62771170771ede584ddc431dac445e43824eaec", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme such that\n(1) all points are closed, and (2) all residue fields are separably\nalgebraically closed. Then\nfor any abelian sheaf <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003> we have\n<MATH_0004> for <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:39c983a5d1d87667c5f0dc79a172cb5979781d111b0bb687417dce44b29de89c", "unit_id": "tag:09AY:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0EZN", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-ring-with-only-minimal-primes}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{cohomology-lemma-vanishing-for-profinite}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-local-dimension-zero-henselian}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-local-rings-strictly-henselian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e23f264061bb1f0c2a3e261205fa58fd93cc50d931282c2c6393f4ff9be13593", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3e62fe96a99aaeb64bbc4eb96d62ce1240b070e481673a6b34af224b68bf53fc", "source_text": "Condition (1) implies that the underlying topological space\nof <MATH_0001> is profinite, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus the higher cohomology groups of an abelian sheaf on the topological\nspace <MATH_0002> (i.e., Zariski cohomology) is trivial, see\nCohomology, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThe local rings are strictly henselian by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThus <ACCENT_0001>tale cohomology of <MATH_0003> is computed by Zariski cohomology\nby Lemma <REF_0004>\nand the proof is done.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8841dc394fb83ed9b472795465c63e3816d04f4f962283d3f6308b9b0b60f10a", "unit_id": "tag:09AY:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0EZN", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-absolutely-integrally-closed-strictly-henselian}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b68d3cb0b14a3ea0d877853870336c1313079dae6f196a11bb4100a854df830c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe spectrum of an absolutely integrally closed ring\nis an example of a scheme all of whose local rings are\nstrictly henselian, see More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nIt turns out that normal domains with separably closed fraction\nfields have an even stronger property as explained in the\nfollowing lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32f7d69c90fc0174bafc504e2fe0dc8ecd3d390ab4cf58e9ee9ef37c80ad28b1", "unit_id": "tag:0EZN:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0EZN", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-normal-scheme-with-alg-closed-function-field}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0ae8b7fed1f7312a219572e3df54d15fc12518d06c4bb63dd10bf8462b73cfd1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:09209c780ac5ea736a97b82e0bac194176ca549872a049f9f3377ccb7b266e2f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an integral normal scheme with separably closed\nfunction field.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A separated <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0002> is a\ndisjoint union of open immersions.\n<STRUCT_0003> All local rings of <MATH_0003> are strictly henselian.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4ba35a3625bf89af6b3c6e24fbb6a2173e54b0137d4815f557e09027b70e2ecf", "unit_id": "tag:09Z9:statement"}
